* ''The two hearths' flow'' (operator, 2026-11-18: //"Mostly pono. Approve all these moves."//; lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/research/two-hearths-flow #/rulings). ''D3'' canon's owner, staged: git owns canon while no Nexus carries it between houses; once a Nexus lives, the floor owns canon and git's `bags/` stands as a generated release mirror of it (genesis bakes from that snapshot); PRs stay for code, and the web3-only law reads GitHub as a web2 bridge behind a causal-island boundary. ''D5'' a merge queue on `develop`: each pull request tests on top of the one ahead, and the push gate reads the queue, never "no run in flight anywhere". ''D6'' a seal merge driver: a `.mem` conflict that touches only `bcc=` seal lines resolves by taking the bodies and re-sealing with `lares meme normalize`. ''D1 and D2'' at their defaults (lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/research/seed-mu): the stood island holds a standing house's ground and the shipped seed stands as an offer and the birth of new houses, one boot line naming both and a "newer seed waits" line printing when engine, grammar or floor differ; `pulama admit` and the kūkulu show the seed-versus-island difference, admission moves nothing, and a separate named act adopts a waiting grammar or engine. D4 (a canon clone for every house) and D7 (the house never writes a working tree) retire under the ruling on workspaces and read-back by descent (lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/state/decisions #/ruled-workspaces); D8 and D10 stand as tools.

